course: dictionary
lesson: 3569
title: Festival
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A festival is a special day or time when people celebrate something, often with traditions, food, music or religious ceremonies. The word can also mean an organised event with lots of performances, like a music festival or a book festival.
explain: «Diwali is the festival of lights, celebrated by Hindus, Sikhs and Jains with lamps, sweets and fireworks.» The clues are lamps, sweets and fireworks. Those are things people do when they celebrate, so a festival is a celebration.
explain: «Bon Odori is a calm circle dance at Japan's summer Obon festival, which honours the spirits of ancestors.» Calm and honours tell you the Obon festival is a time of respect, not just fun. Try swapping in "celebration": "Japan's summer Obon celebration" still makes sense, so the meaning fits.
fact: A festival is a special day or time when people celebrate something.
fact: A festival can also be an organised event with music, performances or activities, such as a film festival.
fact: «Diwali» is the festival of lights, celebrated by Hindus, Sikhs and Jains.
fact: «Zhōngqiū jié» is the Mid-Autumn or Moon Festival, when families look at the full moon and eat mooncake.
fact: Respect other people's festivals; if anyone mocks someone's religion or festival, tell a teacher.
exercise: «Diwali is the festival of lights, celebrated by Hindus, Sikhs and Jains with lamps, sweets and fireworks.» What is a festival? | A test you take at school | A long journey by train | A type of food | *A special day or time when people celebrate
exercise: «Halloween grew from Samhain, an old Celtic festival at the end of the harvest.» Which season was Samhain at the end of? | *Harvest | Spring | Winter snow | Summer holidays
exercise: Ella says a music festival is a quiet day at home. What is a music festival? | A school test about notes | A small party with one singer | A quiet day at home | *An organised event with lots of music and performances
test: «Bon Odori is a calm circle dance at Japan's summer Obon festival.» Which word means peaceful? | circle | Japan's | *calm | summer
test: «In September or October comes Zhōngqiū jié, the Mid-Autumn or Moon Festival.» What is another name for this festival? | Eid al-Fitr | Hanukkah | *Mid-Autumn Festival | Harvest Festival
exam: At a crowded summer festival, what should you do if you might get lost? | *Stay with your group and agree a meeting point beforehand | Wait alone in the car park | Hide behind a food stall | Run off to find the rides alone
